  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Humanitarian Response to the Crisis in G</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CMWU will be responsible for Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene (WASH) Sectoral Objectives: Women, girls, men, and boys across Gaza have improved safe access to lifesaving and sustainable WASH services and improved hygiene practices to safeguard public health.
&#x2022; Phase 1 Activities: Water trucking services, hygiene and Menstrual Hygiene Management (MHM) kit distribution, pprovision of jerry cans, provision of commodes and bedpans, water tank installation with distribution pipelines and emergency tap stands, desalination unit installation, provision of water and sanitation facility operation and maintenance material and tools as well as water testing equipment, installation of emergency sanitation unit (including showers) in IDP centres, institutions and vulnerable communities, hand-washing station installation and conducting household awareness sessions on water borne diseases.
&#x2022; Phase 2 Activities: All activities under Phase 1 with provision/rehabilitation of household sanitation units (latrines and handwashing stations) and household water tanks, installation of appropriate fecal sludge storage and treatment facilities for makeshift IDP settlements, support for community led waste management solutions,
dissemination of information and planning for the prevention and control of public health risks and disease outbreaks.
&#x2022; Phase 3 Activities: All services under Phase 2 with installation/rehabilitation of water transmission pipelines, water and sewer networks and household connections, installation/rehabilitation of stormwater network, lakes, ponds, or rainwater drainage systems, link waste management solutions with public waste management services providers; link public health promotion activities with health service providers, continue any disease outbreak prevention and mitigation activities, establish partnership or coordination mechanisms for community disease surveillance.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="11">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Coastal Municipalities Water Utilit</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Coastal Municipal Water Utility (CMWU) is an autonomous regional water and wastewater utility that provides drinking water supply and wastewater collection and treatment services within their jurisdiction (Rafah area). It is responsible for the construction, operation and maintenance of water extraction and distribution systems; treatment of water sources up to the standards set by PWA; construction, operation and maintenance of sewage infrastructure; and treatment of wastewater up to the standards set by the PWA. CMWU will provide the technical support for the design and rehabilitation supervision of the implementation of desalination plants in addition work with Oxfam and PEF in the community public awareness as well as the water monitoring system.
Oxfam#s partner, CMWU, hasextensive experience in water, desalination and wastewater services, and has implemented projects funded by the European Union and other international agencies in the construction and rehabilitation of desalination plants. Building on this collective experience, the intervention will be the first in Gaza#s unique context with full support of the local government to strictly monitor the water quality of desalinated water in the Gaza strip</narrative>
  </participating-org>
